# Pairs with UniqueOwner. Reproduces current production (#4453): the undo
# clears T's shadow-forward state (lifting its fence) before moving the alias
# back, and arms R's redirect only after the swap. In the first window T serves
# while the alias names R; in the second, R serves while the alias names T.
MODULE: UniqueOwnerUndoClearsBeforeSwap
TARGET: UniqueOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the undo lifts the old copy's fence before the swap and arms the new copy after it, so both serve
PERTURBS: UndoArm, UndoClear

--- FIND
UndoArm ==
    /\ rz \in {"swapped", "retired"}
    /\ alias = R
    /\ redir' = TRUE
    /\ rz' = "undoing"
--- REPLACE
UndoArm ==
\* MUTATION: production order - R is armed last, after the swap.
    /\ rz = "undoing"
    /\ alias = T
    /\ redir' = TRUE
    /\ rz' = "undone"
--- END

--- FIND
UndoClear ==
    /\ rz = "undoing"
    /\ alias = T
    /\ fence' = {}
    /\ rz' = "undone"
--- REPLACE
UndoClear ==
\* MUTATION: production order - T's fence is lifted first, before the swap.
    /\ rz \in {"swapped", "retired"}
    /\ alias = R
    /\ fence' = {}
    /\ rz' = "undoing"
--- END